  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CERF Rapid Response for Grenada and Saint Vincent and the Grenadines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The key economic drivers, including agriculture, fisheries, tourism, and service sectors, have been disrupted, which will impact the livelihood of vulnerable populations. Consequently, this will impact the food security, logistics, nutrition, shelter, and non-food items sectors, particularly among the most vulnerable. Based on the highest wind speed exposure, the number of persons in shelters, and on-the-ground information regarding communities in need, the islands of Union, Carriacou and Petit Martinique are the most affected.&#xa0;This CERF Rapid Response allocation is triggered by the urgent need to address these critical humanitarian needs in the shelter sector in the immediate aftermath of Hurricane Beryl. The allocation will support a swift and coordinated response to prevent further deterioration of the humanitarian situation in the shelter and housing affected and protect the most vulnerable populations in this situation</narrative>
  </description>
